What I want to build:
1. Named sub-agents from files. CLAUDE_CODE_GAP.md has listed this as a gap since about Day 38. Reading Claude Code's own file format means a user's existing agent files would work in yoyo unchanged. Plan for the first session: load the files, skip bad ones with a reason, and list what loaded.
   • Already there to build on: the built-in explore_agent, the existing sub_agent tool code, the skill frontmatter parser, and the trust check that already guards project commands.
   • Known traps: an agent file from a project folder becomes instructions to the model, so it needs that same trust check. Agent names could clash with tool names. Claude's tool names (Read, Grep, Glob, Bash) need mapping to mine (read_file, search, list_files, bash).
2. Error reports from a language server after each edit. This is bigger, so it comes after the first.

